            "title": "Incorrect handling of res.format when only default handler is provided",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/response.js",
            "line": 610,
            "explanation": "Previously, the selection of the matching content type key was done by checking if keys.length is greater than zero and then invoking req.accepts(keys), otherwise setting key to false. The changed line removes the check and directly calls req.accepts(keys), which returns false if keys is empty or no match is found. This change breaks the behavior where if the only handler provided to res.format was 'default', res.format would not fall back correctly since keys would be empty and key would be fal",
            "suggestion": "Restore the original check that if keys.length > 0 then call req.accepts(keys), else set key to false. This ensures correct fallback to default handler if only default is provided."
          }
